  "problem": "Which of the following random variables follows a geometric distribution?\n\nI. The number of cards randomly selected from a deck before selecting a club, if we replace the card after each draw\n\nII. The number of times we randomly select a club from a deck if we pick $10$ cards from a standard deck.\n\nIII. The number of polled people who answered who they voted for in an election until one person says they voted for candidate A",
